  <data key="d36">Escalating tech‑sector geopolitical tensions trigger sanctions, cancelled contracts and rapid divestments that force firms to cut affected business lines and lay off workers in those units.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_security_realignmen</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension_tec" target="global_monetary_tighteni::monetary_policy_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating US‑China tech tensions raise downside growth risk and market volatility, prompting investors to lower the market‑implied future path of policy rates (pricing in slower/harder‑to‑sustain tightening or earlier easing).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension_tec" target="iran_gulf_maritime_tensi::diplomatic_engagement_le" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in US‑China technology rivalry drives China and regional states to step up formal and back‑channel diplomacy with Iran and Gulf partners to secure access, de‑conflict economic links and prevent spillovers into shipping, raising diplomatic engagement levels.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_maritime_tensi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tension_tec" target="russia_ukraine_war::security_coordination" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating US–China technology rivalry reallocates US diplomatic and operational attention and signaling resources toward the Indo‑Pacific, producing slower decision cycles and reduced alignment with European partners on Ukraine assistance and joint planning.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
