  <data key="d36">Sustained energy shortages and higher fuel/utility bills lead energy‑intensive and margin‑squeezed firms to delay investment and recruitment, producing an observable drop in hiring in affected sectors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_security_realignmen</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_monetary_tighteni::cpi_inflation_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Interruptions to oil and natural gas exports raise wholesale energy and transport costs that flow directly into headline consumer prices (fuel, heating, electricity and goods transport), lifting CPI.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_monetary_tighteni::monetary_policy_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained energy-price shocks increase market-implied odds of near-term central-bank tightening as investors price a higher probability of policy responses to contain inflation pressure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="iran_gulf_maritime_tensi::energy_market_risk_premi" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Interruptions to Russian crude and gas flows tighten global balances and raise market perceptions of supply fragility, prompting traders and consumers to add a larger geopolitical risk premium to energy prices that also reflects higher Gulf transit and supply risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_maritime_tensi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="iran_gulf_maritime_tensi::crude_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Actual reductions or delays in Russian crude and refined product availability tighten global supply/demand balances and directly push up benchmark crude prices (spot and near‑term futures), which transmit into Gulf market price levels.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_maritime_tensi</data>
</edge>
