<edge source="iran_gulf_maritime_tensi::shipping_disruption_seve" target="euro_security_realignmen::corporate_cost_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Route closures, port delays and rerouting drive up freight, inventory carrying and just‑in‑time breakdown costs for European manufacturers and retailers, directly raising their operating cost pressure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_maritime_tensi</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_security_realignmen</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_maritime_tensi::shipping_disruption_seve" target="global_monetary_tighteni::cpi_inflation_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Marked disruptions to maritime transit increase delivery times and freight costs for consumer goods and inputs, which firms pass through to retail prices, raising headline consumer inflation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_maritime_tensi</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_maritime_tensi::shipping_disruption_seve" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_logistics_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Severe interruptions to maritime transit (route closures, port delays, higher insurance and rerouting) directly slow or reduce sea shipments of heavy equipment, munitions and fuel destined for Ukraine, degrading military logistics throughput and timeliness.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_maritime_tensi</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_maritime_tensi::shipping_disruption_seve" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::reg_scrutiny_tech" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Severe interruptions to commercial maritime traffic prompt policymakers in the US and allies to broaden and intensify export controls and licensing scrutiny on maritime comms, navigation, and dual‑use components—particularly transfers tied to Chinese firms—raising regulatory oversight of technology transfers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_maritime_tensi</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
